## Why It Matters (HIGH item)

**ARC-005 — Unpinned image (`latest`):** Any registry push replaces the image your runners pull without a Helm/Git change. This silently breaks reproducibility, can introduce a supply-chain compromise, and makes rollbacks impossible. Digest-pinning is the only guarantee of immutability.

---

## Recommended Actions (all fixes go in a Git PR to your Helm values file)

### 1 🔴 Pin the runner image — `ARC-005`
```yaml
# values.yaml
template:
  spec:
    containers:
      - name: runner
        # Replace with the exact digest from your image registry
        image: ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner:2.323.0@sha256:<digest>
```
> Get the digest: `docker buildx imagetools inspect ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner:2.323.0`

---

### 2 🟠 Add a CPU limit — `ARC-010`
```yaml
# values.yaml
template:
  spec:
    containers:
      - name: runner
        resources:
          requests:
            cpu: "500m"
            memory: "1Gi"
          limits:
            cpu: "2000m"   # ← add this; tune to your workload
            memory: "2Gi"
```

---

### 3 🟠 Disable privilege escalation — `ARC-011`
```yaml
# values.yaml
template:
  spec:
    containers:
      - name: runner
        securityContext:
          allowPrivilegeEscalation: false
```

---

### 4 🟡 Add ownership labels — `ARC-013`
```yaml
# values.yaml
labels:
  owner: "platform-team"       # ← your team name
  cost-center: "eng-123"       # ← your cost-center code
```

---

